}

data passive_card_adjacency_is_judged_per_slot_and_by_measurement: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "passive_card_adjacency_is_judged_per_slot_and_by_measurement"),
  decided: "2026-10-30",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "epistemic_humility"),
  provenance: "Operator, relayed by keen-otter-392 from calm-moth-166 and proud-raven to calm-crab-645 on 2026-10-30, correcting gunbc.plans.gpu_card_host_program N0e and N6d (first authored in gunbc#15207): the plan must not blanket-refuse adjacent passive cards. Slot spacing differs between chassis (Butch's is not the H11's), so the authority is per-slot geometry and airflow plus the measured thermal behaviour of the installed position. The H11 incident (96 to 99 C, minimum clocks, a GPU off the bus) stays as evidence for that configuration, not for adjacency itself.",
}

// THE DEFERRAL OF THE UNREACHABLE FLEET READINGS (2026-11-12, fleet_machine_authority P3).
// Six machines could not be observed — srv3 answers ssh and refuses every credential held (measured twice,
// from the session container and from srv1); srv9..srv12 (the DGX Sparks, which have no BMC and so no second
// channel) and host-6ce85c give no route from any read principal held. They are recorded BLOCKED-ON-ACCESS
// with the typed reason, NOT observed and NOT fabricated, and the fleet proceeds on the machines that can be
// read. The trigger that restores a machine is its own reading declaration appearing; until then the row is
// data in gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation::observation_deferrals, and a physical-machine seal for
// a deferred host travels this ruling inside PhysicalMachineAllocationUnobserved. ONE ROW cited by every
// deferral record: six free-text copies could drift, this cannot. The provenance states the decision's real
// authority — an unanswered escalation carried as the recommended default, not an operator instruction.
data fleet_observation_deferral_2026_11_12: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "fleet_observation_deferral_2026_11_12"),
  decided: "2026-11-12",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation", decl_name: "observation_deferrals"),
  provenance: "NOT an operator answer: an escalation raised by vivid-koi-387 on 2026-11-12 — 'P3 SMBIOS reads: srv3 and the Sparks (srv9-srv12) are unreachable. Grant read access, or record them as blocked?' with Defer recommended — went unanswered for 15 minutes, and the dashboard closed it with the recommended option approved by DEFAULT. Defer is therefore applied as an unanswered escalation's default, and this row says so rather than promoting the default to an operator ruling. Its content: record srv3 (ssh answers, refuses every held credential), srv9..srv12 and host-6ce85c (no route from any held read principal; the Sparks have no BMC fallback) as BLOCKED-ON-ACCESS with the typed reason; do not fabricate readings; the fleet proceeds on readable machines; a machine returns to the observed set exactly when its own reading declaration appears in gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation. The blockage itself is measured, not assumed: srv3's key rejection was reproduced twice from two principals, the Sparks and 6ce85c were probed from srv1. Restoring true authority is cheap: a read principal or route appearing, or the operator ratifying or overriding this default.",
}

// THE PERIODIC STANDINGS REFRESH BACKSTOP (2026-11-16). The operator asked for a regular refresh of
// the daily workspace's roadmap standings; the served-observation fold that produces /standings.json
// is otherwise event-driven (a belt tick, fired only on a worker exit or operator action), so an idle
// host freezes the standings and ctrl — which admits roadmap work items against that one document
// (scripts/session-dashboard/lib/roadmap_work_items.mjs parseStandingsResponse/admitWorkspaceWorkItem)
// — sees silently-old data. This ruling is the authority that REOPENS a wall-clock trigger for that
// one fold after dogfood intervention #4 retired the belt timer: the ruling that retired the timer
// (the event-units comment heading gunbc.live_deploy.spec::deployment_belt_exit_path_unit_name,
// "event-driven, not timer-driven") removed the timer that re-WALKED THE FRONTIER
// (spawning/launching/tearing down sessions on a cadence). This ruling does not reverse that. What it
// authorizes is strictly narrower and read-only: a systemd timer that starts a oneshot running ONLY
// `belt_observe_once_cli` — the observation fold, no spawn/launch/teardown — every
// `belt_standings_refresh_backstop` seconds, exactly the mechanism the credential-recovery backstop
// (this module's `belt_credential_recovery_backstop`) already uses for a law with no event to trigger
// it. It also authorizes the freshness law's second, orthogonal 409 gate (`served_observation_standing_of_read`
// age check in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_served_observation): a stored observation older than
// `belt_standings_refresh_staleness_horizon` at read time answers 409 rather than being served 200,
// so a dead timer FAILS CLOSED (ctrl refuses admission) instead of serving bytes whose refresher died.
data refreshes_regularly_every_10_minutes_2026_11_16: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "refreshes_regularly_every_10_minutes_2026_11_16"),
  decided: "2026-11-16",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.belt_cadence", decl_name: "belt_standings_refresh_backstop"),
  provenance: "Operator, relayed by neat-badger-614 to silent-hawk-820 on 2026-11-16, verbatim: \"regarding refreshes - we'd need to build something that refreshes regularly - every 10 minutes or something for now is fine\". Measured at intake: https://srv1.tailecbe08.ts.net:8444/standings.json reported observed_at 2026-11-14T22:51:39Z / log_head fa4a936992b6, ~26h stale, while answering 200 — because no belt tick had run since the last lab worker exited (the lab had no owner since the last lab worker was archived). The operator set the cadence ('every 10 minutes') and its looseness ('or something for now is fine'); the value lives in gunbc.live_deploy.belt_cadence::belt_standings_refresh_backstop (600s), the staleness horizon (derived as three periods from the backstop, in the Second carrier) in belt_standings_refresh_staleness_horizon, and the emitted timer+oneshot pair in gunbc.live_deploy.emit::live_deploy_belt_standings_refresh_\{unit,timer\}_unit_file on the credential-recovery-backstop pattern. The fail-closed 409 age gate is not the operator's request but is required by it: a refresh that silently fails to run would reproduce the exact bug, so the route answers stale itself rather than serving frozen bytes. Approver neat-badger-614 approved the approach with four conditions on 2026-11-16; this row is condition (1) — the ruling recorded in the ledger, not only in a comment.",
}

data t6_fabric_storage_excluded_from_live_deploy_2026_11_10: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "t6_fabric_storage_excluded_from_live_deploy_2026_11_10"),
  decided: "2026-11-10",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "single_authority"),
  provenance: "Operator, relayed by bright-ibex-807 on 2026-11-10 while the T6 runbook (gunb-ai/gunbc#16189, step 2b) was under review, verbatim: \"option B. A small, separate PR first removes the fabric-storage unit from the live deployment's membership (gunbc.live_deploy.spec and whatever emits and applies it), so the modeled deploy (gunbc converge --mode deploy) moves only the five roadmap units and leaves gunbc-roadmap-fabric-storage's fragment and process alone. Keep it in-model: no hand-written unit text, and fabric-storage keeps its existing unit on srv1 untouched.\" ENDS the deployment's ownership of that unit: before this ruling the deployment composed `gunbc-roadmap-fabric-storage.service` (spec.dag deployment_fabric_storage_steps emitted ComposeOwned FabricStorageServeUnit), applied it (apply_legs.dag staged the serialized unit and restarted it), retracted it (retract_legs.dag tore the unit down), and required it as a desired member of the role-singleton realization (role_singleton_convergence.dag missing_members). Two homes then decided one fragment -- the model's emitted ExecStart and the operator's unit on srv1 -- which is the fork gunbc.design_argument::single_authority refuses, and the ruling names the model the home that ends. What the deployment KEEPS, because it is not the unit: the tailscale route to the fabric DB's door socket (ComposeOwned FabricStorageServeMapping), and the store's ownership marker (FabricStorageOwnershipMarker) that pins the fabric DB placement. What it gives up is coverage, recorded here so it is not discovered later: no deploy stages, restarts, retracts or observes that unit any more, so a unit removed or edited by hand on srv1 is no longer a convergence refusal -- it surfaces as a fabric DB request failing at the door socket. The serve mapping still routes to a live service, so the trigger for adding an observation back is a fabric DB endpoint that can be routed to and not answered. The `FabricStorageServeUnit` composition kind stays declared and is REFUSED at both apply and retract (the FleetConvergeTimerUnit precedent in this module), so a spec from an older release that still names the member fails loudly instead of being ignored or torn down. [SUPERSEDED 2026-11-21 by gunbc.design_ruling::fabric_storage_returned_to_live_deploy_supersedes_t6_exclusion_2026_11_21 -- a DEFAULTED escalation, not an operator answer. What was ruled then is recorded here, but the endpoint's unit is deployment state again; that row is the current authority.]",
}

data fabric_storage_returned_to_live_deploy_supersedes_t6_exclusion_2026_11_21: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "fabric_storage_returned_to_live_deploy_supersedes_t6_exclusion_2026_11_21"),
  decided: "2026-11-21",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.spec", decl_name: "deployment_fabric_storage_steps"),
  provenance: "NOT an operator answer. Production was down since 2026-11-21 06:32Z and the operator was not reached; this is the outcome of escalation msg_313db9bd, which closed APPROVED BY DEFAULT after the 15-minute no-answer window on the option 'PR: bring the fabric-storage unit back into the deployment, reversing 11-10'. It is recorded exactly the way gunbc.design_ruling::fleet_observation_deferral_2026_11_12 is recorded -- the operator's silence in that window is recorded as a DEFAULT and is never their assent; a later operator reply or a recorded decision rewrites it. THE DEADLOCK IT ENDS: gunbc.design_ruling::t6_fabric_storage_excluded_from_live_deploy_2026_11_10 (2026-11-10, an operator answer on the record) had made the fabric DB endpoint's systemd unit operator-held and stripped it from the live-deploy membership. The unit on srv1 (gunbc-roadmap-fabric-storage.service) kept running its old `gunbc serve --entry dag/gunbc/fabric/fabric_storage_serve.dag --function fabric_storage_serve_handle --unix-socket .../door.sock` ExecStart; commit 72808ffd2c ('Delete gunbc serve: an entry is served by its deployment binding, realized by gunbc run') then deleted the `serve` subcommand, and the deploy replaces /opt/gunbc/bin/gunbc, so the operator-held unit began crash-looping (read-only ssh on srv1 confirmed it enabled+failed, NRestarts=5, Result exit-code, last start 2026-11-21 06:32:55Z). Every dashboard_deploy then refused at the tailnet-door cutover gate, which reads the fabric journal from that endpoint over the door socket BEFORE handing control over and got HTTP 502 -- and a deploy cannot repair a unit outside its membership, so no deploy could unstick itself (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it). THE DECISION: the endpoint's OWN unit is deployment state again. gunbc.live_deploy.spec composes its name/path and the fabric_storage_ingress_* constants; gunbc.live_deploy.emit live_deploy_fabric_storage_unit_file emits it with the SAME serving invocation the other roadmap units emit after 72808ffd2c -- `gunbc run` on the fabric_storage_ingress binding constructor, handler fabric_storage_serve_handle, over the deployment's fabric door socket (there is no `gunbc serve` any more); gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs deploy_apply_fabric_storage_plan stages AND restarts it BEFORE its tailscale route and so before the cutover gate reads the journal; gunbc.live_deploy.retract_legs tears it down; gunbc.live_deploy.role_singleton_convergence requires it as the FabricUnitMember; gunbc.live_deploy.deploy_artifact_read_sets declares its read-set. The tailscale route (FabricStorageServeMapping) and the store's ownership marker that the 11-10 ruling KEPT under ownership stay unchanged. This row SUPERSEDES t6_fabric_storage_excluded_from_live_deploy_2026_11_10, which stays on the ledger as the record of what was ruled then.",
}

