data dependencies_are_admitted_by_their_consumer: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "dependencies_are_admitted_by_their_consumer"),
  decided: "2026-11-01",
  governs: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "consumption"),
  provenance: "Operator, 2026-11-01, after srv1 hung repeatedly while the board's firmware-first PCIe error handler was taking errors from its unused BMC graphics link: 'if we get 100 things on a board, we are effectively signing up for integration work on everything on that board, unless we disable it, and selectively bring it up -- i would make this the default posture for systems.' Generalized the same day: 'my interest is in proper dependency management -- meaning, we should only use exactly what we need -- in hardware we tend to be lax because we're not sophisticated yet, but as convergence matures, it should head in the direction of being more conservative/diligent', to be aligned at the design level and at each domain. On enabling: 'we have to find a diverse set to expose any integration/diverse mechanisms we otherwise couldn't understand, and then model those, and if they expose any new interactions, disable as much as we can.' First domain application: gunbc.fleet.board_function_admission.",
}

data authorization_pattern_is_a_selection: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
