  provenance: "Operator, on escalation msg_7d9e36b4 (2026-11-15), verbatim: \"Approve enrolment, then accept\", relayed to witty-lark-414 by neat-badger-614 in msg_16d2f3b6-3751-4970-b7c1-550468eca180. It authorizes exactly two rows of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_authored_modules` -- the filesystem absence class's two witnesses, `test.claim.filesystem_read_outcome_witness` and `test.claim.filesystem_absence_establishment_witness`, each admitted at its own name because the class's refusal was enrolled and executed by no lane: the required lane parses and typechecks and judges no claim, so a retired class kept its RED with nothing judging it. Two names and not a family prefix, because a prefix admits every sibling in the namespace, measured or not.",
}

